# umami-backup — analytics DB backup spec for the self-hosted stats box
#
# Companion to umami.compose.example. The site is stateless, but the Umami
# Postgres DB is the ONE launch-surface artifact git can't reproduce — losing
# it means losing funnel history (ANALYTICS.md dashboards, weekly report
# inputs). Keep it boring: nightly pg_dump to a timestamped file, 30-day
# local retention, optional off-box copy.
#
# Install on the stats host (or same VPS, different dir) as root/cron:

# /etc/cron.d/umami-backup
#   m  h dom mon dow user  command
#   17 4 * * *   root  /srv/backup/umami-backup.sh >> /srv/backup/umami.log 2>&1

# /srv/backup/umami-backup.sh
#   #!/usr/bin/env bash
#   set -euo pipefail
#   DIR=/srv/backup/umami
#   mkdir -p "$DIR"
#   TS=$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)
#   # container name matches umami.compose.example's db service
#   docker exec umami-db-1 pg_dump -U umami -d umami \
#     | gzip > "$DIR/umami-$TS.sql.gz"
#   # 30-day retention
#   find "$DIR" -name 'umami-*.sql.gz' -mtime +30 -delete
#   # OPTIONAL off-box copy (owner's choice of destination):
#   # rsync -az "$DIR/umami-$TS.sql.gz" owner@backup-host:/backups/umami/
#
# Restore drill (rehearse once at provisioning, log it in LAUNCH-CHECKLIST §10):
#   gunzip -c /srv/backup/umami/umami-<ts>.sql.gz \
#     | docker exec -i umami-db-1 psql -U umami -d umami
#
# Notes:
# - Contains NO PII beyond what cookieless Umami stores (no IPs persisted by
#   default config); still treat dumps as private — never commit, never ship.
# - A missed night is not an incident; a failed restore is. Verify one dump
#   restores at provisioning time, then spot-check monthly (uptime_probe
#   covers the service, not the backup — check file mtimes in the same cron
#   mail/log review).
# - Cheaper standing guard, no docker needed: append
#     && /path/to/tools/backup_verify.sh latest /srv/backup/umami
#   to the cron line — it fails (and mails via cron MAILTO) if the newest
#   dump is stale, corrupt, or a hollow non-pg_dump file.
# - If analytics lands on a hosted Plausible/Umami cloud instead (G8
#   alternative), this file is moot — export via the provider's tools.
